# Offline vdW-DF2 (LMKLL) pin notes — gpw-vdw-df2-ice

## Kernel oracle (libvdwxc)

CP2K `VDW_POTENTIAL NON_LOCAL TYPE LMKLL` uses the same Román–Pérez–Soler
kernel family as **libvdwxc DF2**. DF1 and DF2 share the default RPS kernel
tables; the functional difference is only \(Z_{ab}\) in \(q_0\):

| Functional | CP2K TYPE | libvdwxc | \(Z_{ab}\) |
| ---------- | --------- | -------- | ---------- |
| vdW-DF     | DRSLL     | DF1      | −0.8491    |
| vdW-DF2    | LMKLL     | DF2      | −1.887     |

Hard unit-test pin is libvdwxc 0.5.0 on a fixed synthetic density (not live
in ctest):

```text
# 16^3 cubic L=8 Bohr, rho = exp(-0.5 r^2) blob at center, analytic sigma
E_nl DRSLL/DF1 = 1.2367739353586621e-01 Ha
E_nl LMKLL/DF2 = 1.1428161716669384e-01 Ha
```

Pin harness (serial libvdwxc + FFTW3):

```bash
gcc -O2 pin_vdw_df2.c -I$LIBVDWXC/include -L$LIBVDWXC/lib -lvdwxc -lfftw3 -lm
# functional=VDWXC_DF2 (2)
```

## Full GPW regression pin

Post-SCF \(E_c^{\mathrm{nl}}\) on Γ-PBE density of the water dimer
(CUTOFF 200 Ry, DZVP-MOLOPT-SR-GTH, 12 Å cell):

```text
E_disp = 1.3011875519702767e-01 Ha
```

## Suggested CP2K twin (when QS + libvdwxc available)

```
&FORCE_EVAL
  METHOD Quickstep
  &DFT
    &XC
      &XC_FUNCTIONAL PBE &END XC_FUNCTIONAL
      &VDW_POTENTIAL
        POTENTIAL_TYPE NON_LOCAL
        &NON_LOCAL
          TYPE LMKLL
          CUTOFF_RC  0.0   ! use default kernel mesh
        &END NON_LOCAL
      &END VDW_POTENTIAL
    &END XC
    &MGRID CUTOFF 200 &END MGRID
    &QS METHOD GPW &END QS
    &SCF  ...  &END SCF
  &END DFT
  &SUBSYS
    ! water dimer geometry as REFERENCE.md
  &END SUBSYS
&END FORCE_EVAL
```

Record `Dispersion energy` / nonlocal XC contribution and CP2K version in
REFERENCE.md when a host provides a fair twin wall.
